# Patterns here are in addition to .gitignore and repomix's built-in
# binary-file detection. Goal: ship only what helps an LLM reason about
# the code — drop binaries, generated output, and oversized historical docs.

# --- Binary / media assets (also caught by binary detection, listed for clarity) ---
docs/assets/
*.gif
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.mp4
*.mov
*.glb
*.gltf
*.ply
*.obj
*.fbx
*.stl

# --- Historical planning docs (huge, low value for code context) ---
# Keep specs/ — those describe the current design. Drop plans/ — they're
# the long implementation log and balloon the pack.
docs/superpowers/plans/

# --- Pipeline run outputs (generated, may contain large artifacts) ---
runs/
**/runs/

# --- Python tooling caches & build artifacts (belt-and-suspenders vs .gitignore) ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# --- Lockfiles (rarely useful to an LLM; large and noisy) ---
uv.lock
poetry.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock

# --- Editor / OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Repomix's own output, in case it's ever generated in-repo ---
repomix-output.*
